==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Macho Suntan Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Permed Suntan Cat ''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Suntan Cat is a meatshield created almost specifically to combat [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies, his 50% chance to [[Dodge Attack|dodge]] their attacks finding great use, as a lot of weak peons and strong pushers also tend to be Traitless. However, if he doesn't dodge, he will be destroyed immediately, and he obviously can't handle enemies with traits.

Due to relying only on the Dodge ability, there is not much reason to level Suntan Cat up unless you want to unlock his True Form, especially considering how expensive he is as a Super Rare.

==='''True Form'''===
Permed Suntan Cat gains increased health and speed. The HP boost allows Permed Suntan Cat to tank a few more hits from some enemies and thus gain more chances to dodge. However, stronger enemies can punch right through that boosted HP outside of a dodge, so this is relegated to stages where weak peons such as [[Doge]] or [[Squire Rel]] can be used to land several hits on him to give him several chances to dodge a powerful hit from a more powerful enemy, and even that would depend on luck and low buffs on the peons. Furthermore, this increase in HP is too little to help on mixed stages.

The increased speed helps him somewhat, as he can now reach the front lines faster after being deployed. While this does mean that there is less space between each Permed Suntan Cat, it's often not an issue as he is rarely expected to be the main meatshield in any stage and is only meant to be used in conjunction with other, more spammable meatshields. Overall, this True Form is somewhat of an improvement if you could pay up for it, but might not be worth the XP and Catfruit requirement if you're short on these.

